PRIVATE REFLECTION: {The question requires identifying which Hfr origin + polarity places azi as the clearly proximal/earliest marker (hence “prolonged expression before others”). Standard circular order (clockwise increasing min): thr(0)–leu–azi(~2)–ton(~3)–pro–lac–str(~73). azi is first-transferred only if oriT lies immediately “upstream” of azi and transfer heads toward it, i.e., either (a) ori near ton + counterclockwise (ton→azi→leu→thr) or (b) ori between leu/azi + clockwise (azi first, then long arc).  
Group split: 11 colleagues favor A (origin near ton), arguing proximity alone suffices and that conventional labeling sometimes swaps the word “clockwise”; 4 favor D (origin near thr, counterclockwise), arguing that places azi early relative to distant markers. Both sets contain internal contradictions on polarity vs. map direction.  
No other option (lac, pro, str) can ever make azi proximal. Persistent open issue: exact wording of each option’s direction label versus the physical map. Current best-supported choice remains A on majority + proximity reasoning, but D is the only polarity that is topologically correct for a ton-proximal origin.}

